Subject: WPE on Phoenix: native HLS in the FFmpeg media player, MediaCapabilities answers

<video src=*.m3u8> as Safari plays it (coordination repo docs/browser/MSE-DESIGN.md, stage 0),
on top of patch 0030's player (platform/graphics/ffmpeg/, BSD-2-Clause):

  FFmpegHLSSession   FFmpeg's hls demuxer on a context whose io_open/io_close2 are the
                     session's: every media playlist (and live reload), init section, segment
                     and key becomes an FFmpegMediaStream, a request of WebKit's media
                     resource loader (cookies, TLS, CORS, cache: the browser's; FFmpeg stays
                     --disable-network, the video_player port's hls.c hunk names http(s) URLs
                     under custom I/O). Media playlists are read whole (<= 1 MiB), their URIs
                     made absolute against the response URL, refused when encrypted with
                     anything but AES-128/identity (SAMPLE-AES, DRM key formats), and served
                     from memory; AES-128 segments are decrypted here (av_aes, CBC, PKCS#7);
                     EXT-X-BYTERANGE segments are Range requests; segment streams share the
                     player's read-ahead budget.
  FFmpegMediaPolicy  plain C++ (host-tested): RFC 6381 codec strings, the decoding table
                     (HEVC 8-bit <= 1080p30: supported, smooth, power-efficient -- the rpivid
                     block; H.264 <= 720p30 supported and smooth; HEVC Main10 and larger H.264
                     supported, not smooth; no AV1, Dolby Vision, HDR, VP9 above profile 0 or
                     360p), master/media playlist parsing, the variant choice (HEVC 8-bit
                     <= 1080p30, else H.264 <= 720p30, else HEVC Main10, else the lowest
                     decodable; ties: lower BANDWIDTH; the DEFAULT audio rendition) and the
                     single-variant master the demuxer gets (given the real one it would open
                     and probe every rendition)
  PlatformMediaEngineConfigurationFactoryFFmpeg
                     MediaCapabilities.decodingInfo() from that table (it answered
                     supported:false for everything: no factory without Cocoa/GStreamer);
                     Media Source configurations only with ENABLE(MEDIA_SOURCE)

MediaPlayerPrivateFFmpeg: HLS by MIME type (application/vnd.apple.mpegurl, application/x-mpegurl,
application/mpegurl, audio/mpegurl, audio/x-mpegurl -- now in the engine's types, so canPlayType
answers "maybe", "probably" with decodable codecs), by an .m3u8/.m3u path or by a body starting
#EXTM3U. VOD: duration = the playlist's, seekable; live (no end list): duration +Infinity,
LiveStream, not seekable (seeks resolve at the current time). The decoders open at the first
play(), not at the metadata: an HLS player that never plays holds no decoder and never takes the
rpivid block; it reports HaveEnoughData meanwhile (autoplay, 'canplay'), seeks complete at once
and apply at play, and below preload="auto" its demuxer is closed after the metadata (no segment
open). The stream probe decodes on the CPU (rpivid=0) for the same reason. A picture queue that
runs dry while playing holds the clock (readyState HaveCurrentData: 'waiting'; a "rebuffer"),
a pts jump of more than a second (EXT-X-DISCONTINUITY) moves the clock to it. H.264 decodes with
3 threads in HLS mode. canPlayType codec answers come from FFmpegMediaPolicy (rejects av01, dvh1,
dvhe, vp09.02, HEVC range extensions; accepts ac-3/ec-3); container types match case-blind.

FFmpegMediaStream: created on any thread (requests still start on the main thread), byte ranges
(Range: bytes=start-end, a server ignoring it is cut at the end), the response URL (redirects),
a buffer of the resource's size when that is below the read-ahead window and a small first one
when the size is unknown, peek() for the #EXTM3U sniff.

Logs ("WPEB-MEDIA ..."): canplaytype type= platform= answer=, capabilities type= codec=
<w>x<h>@<fps> audio= supported= smooth= efficient=, hls master/policy/variant i=/choose i= rule=
audio=, hls live= segments= target=, hls playlist/reload/open (rate-limited), hls idle/opened,
rebuffer start/end, discontinuity, error hls-*; the stat line gains (HLS only) hls=1 variant= rule=
vcodec= res= bw= live= segments=<opened>/<in playlist> reloads= rebuffers= hls_streams= hls_kb=
idle=. Knobs: WPE_PHOENIX_HLS_VARIANT=<i>, WPE_PHOENIX_HLS_POLICY=lowest|highest,
WPE_PHOENIX_HLS_HEVC_MAX=WxH, WPE_PHOENIX_HLS_H264_MAX=WxH, WPE_PHOENIX_HLS_HEVC_MAX_FPS=<n>.

